{"headword":"שֵׂעִיר","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.pr. Sēʿîr (</strong>= <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂעִיר</span> <em>goat?</em> cf. Gray<sup>Prop. N. 94</sup>; but note play in <span dir=\"rtl\">שֵׂעָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 25:25\" href=\"/Genesis.25.25\">Gn 25:25</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂעִר</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:11\" href=\"/Genesis.27.11\">27:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 27:23\" href=\"/Genesis.27.23\">23</a>; Nö<sup>ZMG xl (1886), 165; Ency. Bib. ii. 1183</sup> cp. n.pr. mont. <span dir=\"rtl\">الاشعر</span> (the ‘hairy,’ i.e. ‘well-wooded,’ cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">شَعَارٌ</span> <em>trees</em>), n.pr.gent. (orig.n.pr.loc.) <span dir=\"rtl\">أَلَاشْعَرُ</span>; Lag<sup>BN 92</sup> thinks <span dir=\"rtl\">שׂ׳</span> orig.n.pr.m., but land much earlier in OT; perhaps = TelAm. land <em>Šêri</em>, Zim<sup>ZA vi (1891), 257</sup> Jastr<sup>JBL xi (1892), 114</sup> Wkl<sup>TelAm. 181, 26</sup> Buhl<sup>Edom. 28 f.</sup><strong>)</strong>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Σηειρ:"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong> terr.</strong> land of Edom, S. of Dead Sea, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַ֫רְצָה שׂ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 32:4\" href=\"/Genesis.32.4\">Gn 32:4</a> (J; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׂדֵה אֱדוֹם</span>), cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 36:30\" href=\"/Genesis.36.30\">36:30</a> (P); <span dir=\"rtl\">שׂ׳</span> alone <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:4\" href=\"/Judges.5.4\">Ju 5:4</a> (poem; ‖ id.), <a data-ref=\"Numbers 24:18\" href=\"/Numbers.24.18\">Nu 24:18</a> (JE; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אֱדוֹם</span>), <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:44\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.44\">Dt 1:44</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.4\">2:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:12\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.22\">22</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:29\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.29\">29</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deutero